    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\r\n\r\nMoves from M-FSDP to GTP for Nemotron 3 Ultra recipes on GB200 and GB300. GTP has better support for checkpointing, and is also convergence tested, along with better support for CUDA Graphs.\r\n\r\n# Changelog\r\n\r\n- Introduced _apply_nemotron_3_ultra_gtp function to configure GTP settings for dense weight sharding.\r\n\r\n- Updated nemotron_3_ultra_pretrain_256gpu_gb200_fp8mx_config and nemotron_3_ultra_pretrain_256gpu_gb300_fp8mx_config to apply GTP settings.\r\n\r\n- Added support for GTP sharding in the moe_latent_proj module to address memory pressure.\r\n\r\n# GitHub Actions CI\r\n\r\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\r\n\r\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\r\n\r\n**Pre checks**:\r\n\r\n- [ ] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [ ] Did you write any new necessary tests?\r\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\r\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\r\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\r\n\r\nIf you haven't finished some of the above items you can still open \"Draft\" PR.\r\n\r\n# Additional Information\r\n\r\n- Related to # (issue)\r\n",
